CODEGEN.md §5.4, DECISIONS 279(c): a row's `id` and `retired` are written only where the value sits in a table, never because the record is a row type: the elements of a keyed list of a record that is also a table's row have neither. Mode baked.
-- a/a.canon --
/// Rows that are also keyed-list elements.
package a

/// An item.
record Item {
  /// Its sku.
  sku: String
}

/// Extra items, a table.
let extra: table Item = { one { sku: "one" } }

/// Items, a keyed list of the same record.
let items: [Item] keyed by sku = [ { sku: "i1" } ]

emit ts { out: "@features/a/a.ts", mode: baked }
